+## Colour-token architecture
+
+`styles/tokens.css` is the Player colour-system owner. Canonical palette values use `oklch()`. Numbered neutral and
+accent primitives follow a Radix-inspired 12-step functional progression, while Player components consume semantic
+roles such as `--surface-component`, `--border-interactive`, and `--accent-solid`. Radix is design guidance only; the
+Player has no Radix, React, palette-runtime, or generated-Radix-CSS dependency.
+
+The approved light-theme anchors below are compatibility references for the current appearance. Their canonical values
+are the OKLCH primitives in `styles/tokens.css`; the HEX values are not the design source.
+
+| Semantic role | sRGB reference |
+| --- | --- |
+| `surface-base` | `#F7F0E8` |
+| `surface-chrome` | `#FCF6EF` |
+| `surface-component` | `#FFFCF7` |
+| `component-hover` | `#F8EEE5` |
+| `component-pressed` | `#F2E3D8` |
+| `border-subtle` | `#D9C8B8` |
+| `border-interactive` | `#CBB2A1` |
+| `border-strong` | `#B49380` |
+| `text-primary` | `#382D2A` |
+| `text-muted` | `#79665F` |
+| `accent-focus` / application UI accent | `#E84C71` |
+| `accent-solid` | `#D63B61` |
+| `accent-solid-hover` | `#C93659` |
+| `accent-solid-pressed` | `#B82F4F` |
+| `disabled-bg` | `#EFE6DF` |
+| `disabled-border` | `#DECFC4` |
+| `disabled-text` | `#8A7770` |
+
+The tool-column body and header both render on `surface-component`; the container owns that surface and the header
+remains transparent so the same colour is not double-painted at its rounded outer edge. The selector, add, and close
+controls are component surfaces as well. Neutral controls use `border-subtle` by default, `border-interactive` on hover, and `border-strong`
+for pressed or deliberately stronger neutral emphasis. Package/speaker/media identity remains separate from application
+accent semantics. No dark palette is approved yet; a future dark theme should replace the theme mappings rather than
+rewrite component styles or invert the light palette automatically.
+
 No UI or CSS framework is required by this POC. Presentation data, rendering, panel transitions, and browser bootstrap are separate seams so a later runtime integration or UI-framework decision does not become part of the presentation contract by accident.
 
